A vintage 1960s travel poster style illustration depicting a steaming cup of dark coffee in the foreground, with a dreamy split landscape behind it: on one side, terraced coffee plantations climbing misty Javanese volcanic hills with traditional Indonesian architecture, on the other side, Vietnamese highland coffee farms with conical hat-wearing farmers among the rows. The scene is bathed in warm sepia and amber tones, with weathered paper texture and slightly faded colors reminiscent of old European travel advertisements. Soft morning mist weaves between the mountains, and coffee plant branches with ripe red cherries frame the composition elegantly.
